{"files":[{"additions":4,"blob_url":"https://github.com/wstein/gramaire/blob/dc111a9212654b95ee05b64eba3ccb0ad50dc8e8/site%2Fsrc%2Fcontent%2Fdocs%2Fdocs%2Foverview.mdx","changes":4,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wstein/gramaire/contents/site%2Fsrc%2Fcontent%2Fdocs%2Fdocs%2Foverview.mdx?ref=dc111a9212654b95ee05b64eba3ccb0ad50dc8e8","deletions":0,"filename":"site/src/content/docs/docs/overview.mdx","patch":"@@ -14,5 +14,9 @@ a verdict from one matches the other.\n \n - **New to Gramaire?** Start with the [tutorial](../../tutorials/intro/) — it\n   builds a small calculator grammar from scratch.\n+- **Curious why the project looks the way it does?** See\n+  [where Gramaire is headed](../why-gramaire/) — the shift from proving a\n+  self-hosting engine to interchange-format credibility and the Gramaire\n+  Notebook.\n - **Want the formal rules?** See the [language specification](../specs/grammar-format/).\n - **Looking for a schema or contract artifact?** See the [schema overview](../specs/schema-overview/).","raw_url":"https://github.com/wstein/gramaire/raw/dc111a9212654b95ee05b64eba3ccb0ad50dc8e8/site%2Fsrc%2Fcontent%2Fdocs%2Fdocs%2Foverview.mdx","sha":"04f735557a35bcafa459483e38db2f84b5e81af3","status":"modified"},{"additions":77,"blob_url":"https://github.com/wstein/gramaire/blob/dc111a9212654b95ee05b64eba3ccb0ad50dc8e8/site%2Fsrc%2Fcontent%2Fdocs%2Fdocs%2Fwhy-gramaire.mdx","changes":77,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wstein/gramaire/contents/site%2Fsrc%2Fcontent%2Fdocs%2Fdocs%2Fwhy-gramaire.mdx?ref=dc111a9212654b95ee05b64eba3ccb0ad50dc8e8","deletions":0,"filename":"site/src/content/docs/docs/why-gramaire.mdx","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@\n+---\n+title: Where Gramaire is headed\n+description: Why Gramaire's focus has shifted from proving a self-hosting engine to building the product around it — interchange-format credibility, a live Notebook, and a planned rebrand.\n+---\n+\n+import { Aside, CardGrid, LinkCard } from \"@astrojs/starlight/components\";\n+\n+Gramaire started as an internal proof: could a grammar notation describe\n+itself well enough to bootstrap its own parser generator? That question is\n+answered — the self-hosting loop (lexer → canonical LR(1) → LALR/IELR →\n+generated codegen → parsing its own grammar spec back) is done and stable,\n+with an ALL(\\*)/PEG side-engine and several Scala backend targets layered on\n+top of it since. The project's center of gravity has moved on to what that\n+engine is actually _for_. Three things are happening in parallel now.\n+\n+## Earning credibility as an interchange format\n+\n+Rather than asserting Gramaire is \"the standard\" EBNF-family format, the plan\n+is to prove it — with real round-trips through established tools. ANTLR was\n+first; Bison/yacc is the one most recently finished. The bar isn't \"it\n+parses\": it's `import(export(x))` fidelity — a `.g4` or `.y` grammar\n+imported into Gramaire and exported back out should be the same grammar, not\n+an approximation of it.\n+\n+## Becoming a learning and debugging platform\n+\n+Most of the recent work isn't in the CLI at all — it's the **Gramaire\n+Notebook**, a standalone, live-editing, in-browser surface where a grammar\n+is a real document: you edit it, get located error/warning squiggles on the\n+exact broken cell, see railroad diagrams with action badges for every rule,\n+and try it against real input via a calculator built from the grammar's own\n+`{% %}` actions. That's a materially different product shape than \"run a\n+CLI, get a parser\" — the Notebook is meant to be where you _understand_ a\n+grammar, not just where you compile one.\n+\n+<LinkCard\n+  title=\"Try the Gramaire Notebook\"\n+  href=\"/notebook/\"\n+  description=\"Click any cell to edit it — the railroad diagrams and FIRST/FOLLOW tables update live, against the real engine.\"\n+/>\n+\n+## A planned identity change to match\n+\n+<Aside type=\"note\" title=\"Not yet in effect\">\n+  This is a planned, gated change — nothing on the site has been renamed yet. It\n+  ships as a full redesign before a general-availability release, not a\n+  find-and-replace.\n+</Aside>\n+\n+The project intends to rebrand **Gramaire → Gramaire**, specifically because\n+of this shift. \"Gramaire\" shares the root _gramaire_ with \"grammar\" — it\n+names a book you write living things into, which fits a live notebook in a\n+way the old grammar-plus-Markdown pun (\"Gra-m-ark\") never had to. The\n+Gramaire Notebook already carries the name today, ahead of the rest of the\n+rebrand, because it's the one part of the product this new identity was\n+coined to describe.\n+\n+## Where this leaves the fundamentals\n+\n+None of this changes what already works. The three parse-table methods\n+(canonical LR(1), LALR(1), IELR(1)), the single-file `.gram.md` format, and\n+the self-hosting loop are the foundation the interchange-format work and the\n+Notebook are both built on — they're not being replaced, just no longer the\n+whole story.\n+\n+<CardGrid>\n+  <LinkCard\n+    title=\"Getting started\"\n+    href=\"/tutorials/intro/\"\n+    description=\"Build a small calculator grammar from scratch, in about ten minutes.\"\n+  />\n+  <LinkCard\n+    title=\"Try the Lab\"\n+    href=\"/lab/\"\n+    description=\"Edit a grammar and inspect its parse tables, conflicts, and parse trace directly.\"\n+  />\n+</CardGrid>","raw_url":"https://github.com/wstein/gramaire/raw/dc111a9212654b95ee05b64eba3ccb0ad50dc8e8/site%2Fsrc%2Fcontent%2Fdocs%2Fdocs%2Fwhy-gramaire.mdx","sha":"e7cdfb719752bca23bc11187783897d34b72eb3c","status":"added"},{"additions":6,"blob_url":"https://github.com/wstein/gramaire/blob/dc111a9212654b95ee05b64eba3ccb0ad50dc8e8/site%2Fsrc%2Fpages%2Findex.astro","changes":11,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wstein/gramaire/contents/site%2Fsrc%2Fpages%2Findex.astro?ref=dc111a9212654b95ee05b64eba3ccb0ad50dc8e8","deletions":5,"filename":"site/src/pages/index.astro","patch":"@@ -115,27 +115,28 @@ const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;\n     </div>\n \n     <div class=\"tiles\">\n-      <FeatureTile\n-        big=\"3×\"\n-        small=\"parse-table methods — canonical LR(1), LALR(1), IELR(1)\"\n-      />\n       <FeatureTile\n         big=\"1 file\"\n         small=\"grammar and docs are the same .gram.md\"\n       />\n+      <FeatureTile\n+        big=\"round-trip\"\n+        small=\"ANTLR and Bison/yacc import↔export, byte-for-byte — an interchange format proven, not just claimed\"\n+      />\n       <FeatureTile\n         big=\"closed\"\n         small=\"the self-hosting loop — it reads its own notation back\"\n       />\n       <FeatureTile\n         big=\"Notebook\"\n-        small=\"prose, grammar cells, and live outputs in one scrolling document — the Gramaire Notebook\"\n+        small=\"prose, grammar cells, and live outputs in one scrolling document — a place to learn and debug a grammar, not just generate one\"\n       />\n     </div>\n \n     <footer class=\"footer\">\n       <span>Gramaire · Apache-2.0</span>\n       <a href={`${base}docs/overview/`}>Docs</a>\n+      <a href={`${base}docs/why-gramaire/`}>Where we're headed</a>\n       <a href={`${base}tutorials/intro/`}>Tutorial</a>\n       <a href={`${base}lab/`}>Lab</a>\n       <a href={`${base}notebook/`}>Notebook</a>","raw_url":"https://github.com/wstein/gramaire/raw/dc111a9212654b95ee05b64eba3ccb0ad50dc8e8/site%2Fsrc%2Fpages%2Findex.astro","sha":"a7a83ca0c17f45914364017a7a80ccd9afb3c8b1","status":"modified"},{"additions":0,"blob_url":"https://github.com/wstein/gramaire/blob/dc111a9212654b95ee05b64eba3ccb0ad50dc8e8/site%2Ftests%2Fvisual%2Fshell.spec.ts-snapshots%2Fdocs-overview-dark-chromium-darwin.png","changes":0,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wstein/gramaire/contents/site%2Ftests%2Fvisual%2Fshell.spec.ts-snapshots%2Fdocs-overview-dark-chromium-darwin.png?ref=dc111a9212654b95ee05b64eba3ccb0ad50dc8e8","deletions":0,"filename":"site/tests/visual/shell.spec.ts-snapshots/docs-overview-dark-ch